    "rationale": "Twenty modules bound by the digest of their bytes at R6, verified from Git objects rather than the working tree. R6 changes stream completion semantics in the relay: a response is complete when it delivers its terminal event or its declared length, not when the socket closes. Under v4 the relay presented a truncated stream to its client as HTTP 200 with no recorded failure, so a fragment and a short answer were indistinguishable to anything downstream of it."
  },
